From: Spaceghost <Spaceghost@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 08:25:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] create_inode: use source mtime for reproducible ctime

Buildroot can normalize source-tree mtimes for reproducible images, but a
normal touch cannot set ctime.  Copying the host ctime into every populated
inode therefore makes otherwise identical ext filesystems differ on every
build.

When SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH is present, use the already-normalized source mtime as
the inode ctime too.  Preserve the existing behavior for ordinary mke2fs use.

---
 misc/create_inode.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/misc/create_inode.c b/misc/create_inode.c
index 8a2f64f..6307c9a 100644
--- a/misc/create_inode.c
+++ b/misc/create_inode.c
@@ -127,7 +127,10 @@ static errcode_t set_inode_extra(ext2_filsys fs, ext2_ino_t ino,
 	inode.i_mode = (LINUX_S_IFMT & inode.i_mode) | (~S_IFMT & st->st_mode);
 	inode.i_atime = st->st_atime;
 	inode.i_mtime = st->st_mtime;
-	inode.i_ctime = st->st_ctime;
+	if (getenv("SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH"))
+		inode.i_ctime = st->st_mtime;
+	else
+		inode.i_ctime = st->st_ctime;
 
 	retval = ext2fs_write_inode(fs, ino, &inode);
 	if (retval)
-- 
2.39.5
